        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents,skills): keep session-identity and experience-review transcript truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`normalizeCliContextValue` (cli-output.ts) and `formatSkillExperienceReviewTranscript` (experience-review-prompt.ts) use raw `.slice(0, N)` / `.slice(-N)` to truncate user-visible strings. When a truncation boundary falls inside a UTF-16 surrogate pair (e.g. emoji), the result contains a lone surrogate — `encodeURIComponent()` throws `URIError: URI malformed`, JSON serialisers may reject the string, and downstream display surfaces render broken characters.\n\nThe codebase already applies `truncateUtf16Safe` / `sliceUtf16Safe` in 30+ locations (#98644, #102470, #101728, #104800, etc.). These two truncation sites were missed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`normalizeCliContextValue` truncates session_id/run_id for error message formatting in `formatCliOutputError`. `formatSkillExperienceReviewTranscript` truncates rendered LLM conversation output for skill review prompts. Both receive arbitrary Unicode content from users/models.\n\nThe fix follows the established pattern — replace raw `.slice(0, N)` with `truncateUtf16Safe`, and `full.slice(-tailBudget)` with `sliceUtf16Safe(full, tailStart)`. Same approach as #98644 (ZengWen-DT) and #102470 (zw-xysk).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Error messages from `formatCliOutputError` no longer produce broken characters at emoji boundaries\n- Skill experience review transcripts no longer corrupt emoji at truncation boundaries\n- Affected strings survive `encodeURIComponent` / `JSON.stringify` / UTF-8 disk write without throwing\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Environment**: Node.js v24.13.1, @openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice, Linux x86_64, upstream/main at bd2be839c.\n\n**Scenario 1 — normalizeCliContextValue** (CLI session_id straddling emoji at 200-char boundary):\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx -e '\nimport { truncateUtf16Safe } from \"@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice\";\nconst id = \"s\".repeat(199) + \"😀tail\";\nconst before = id.slice(0, 200);\nconst after  = truncateUtf16Safe(id, 200);\nconst last = (s) => JSON.stringify(s.slice(-5));\nconsole.log(\"before:\", last(before), \"len:\", before.length);\nconsole.log(\"after:\",  last(after),  \"len:\", after.length);\ntry { encodeURIComponent(before); console.log(\"encodeURIComponent(before): ok\"); }\ncatch (e) { console.log(\"encodeURIComponent(before):\", e.message); }\ntry { encodeURIComponent(after); console.log(\"encodeURIComponent(after): ok\"); }\ncatch (e) { console.log(\"encodeURIComponent(after):\", e.message); }\n'\n```\n\n```\nbefore: \"ssss\\ud83d\" len: 200          ← lone high surrogate at end\nafter:  \"sssss\" len: 199               ← safely truncated before emoji\nencodeURIComponent(before): URI malformed ← crashes\nencodeURIComponent(after): ok             ← passes\n```\n\n**Scenario 2 — experience-review first message** (`.slice(0, 6000)` bisecting emoji):\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx -e '\nimport { truncateUtf16Safe } from \"@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice\";\nconst content = \"[user]\\n\" + \"a\".repeat(5992) + \"😀rest\";\nconst before = content.slice(0, 6000);\nconst after  = truncateUtf16Safe(content, 6000);\nconst hasDangling = (s) => /[\\uD800-\\uDBFF](?![\\uDC00-\\uDFFF])|(?<![\\uD800-\\uDBFF])[\\uDC00-\\uDFFF]/u.test(s);\nconsole.log(\"before len:\", before.length, \"dangling:\", hasDangling(before), \"tail:\", JSON.stringify(before.slice(-2)));\nconsole.log(\"after  len:\", after.length,  \"dangling:\", hasDangling(after),  \"tail:\", JSON.stringify(after.slice(-2)));\n'\n```\n\n```\nbefore len: 6000 dangling: true tail: \"a\\ud83d\"   ← lone high surrogate\nafter  len: 5999 dangling: false tail: \"aa\"       ← safe\n```\n\n**Scenario 3 — experience-review tail** (`.slice(-tailBudget)` starting at low surrogate):\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx -e '\nimport { sliceUtf16Safe } from \"@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice\";\nconst full = \"a\".repeat(10000) + \"🦞\" + \"b\".repeat(100);\nconst tailBudget = 101; const start = full.length - tailBudget;\nconst before = full.slice(-tailBudget);\nconst after  = sliceUtf16Safe(full, start);\nconst hasDangling = (s) => /[\\uD800-\\uDBFF](?![\\uDC00-\\uDFFF])|(?<![\\uD800-\\uDBFF])[\\uDC00-\\uDFFF]/u.test(s);\nconsole.log(\"start:\", start, \"full[10000]:\", JSON.stringify(full[10000]), \"full[10001]:\", JSON.stringify(full[10001]));\nconsole.log(\"before first:\", JSON.stringify(before[0]), \"dangling:\", hasDangling(before));\nconsole.log(\"after  first:\", JSON.stringify(after[0]),  \"dangling:\", hasDangling(after));\n'\n```\n\n```\nstart: 10001 full[10000]: \"\\ud83e\" full[10001]: \"\\udd9e\"  ← 🦞 spans [10000]-[10001]\nbefore first: \"\\udd9e\" dangling: true                      ← starts with lone low surrogate\nafter  first: \"b\"      dangling: false                     ← aligned ✅\n```\n\n**Unit tests**:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/cli-output.test.ts src/skills/workshop/experience-review.test.ts\n```\n\n```\nTest Files  3 passed (3)\n     Tests  158 passed (158)\n```\n\n**Diff**: 4 files, +65/-3. No pnpm-lock.yaml. Branch from upstream/main (bd2be839c).\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
